Improve benign/false-positive discrimination — Status: NOT STARTED / SUGGESTED\n- TEST 3 (Benign Control with parameterized SQL `%s`) still triggers a false positive even after calibrated retraining. The model flags safe parameterized queries as SQL injection. More benign training samples or higher weighting may be needed in a future training iteration.\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n- **User GitHub/HF identity:** `k4ran909`, email `k4ran909@gmail.com`, name Karan\n- **Colab notebook URL:** `https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1u6mCyiyeT45QW6O0L-95tJ-csN6VEC17`\n- **HF Model Repo:** `k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` — https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\n- **Workspace:** `c:\\Users\\k4ran\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\smartAGENT`\n- **CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (user-enforced):** Absolutely zero mention of legacy base model names (\"Qwen\", \"qwen2\", \"Alibaba\") anywhere in code, markdown, configurations, datasets, or outputs.\n- **Zero Ollama dependency** — model runs via Unsloth/transformers only.\n- **User pattern:** Says \"do it for me\" — expects full automated execution, not instructions. Uses `/browser` and `/goal` slash commands for browser automation tasks.\n- **User approved** the calibrated retraining plan (r=16, α=32, 25 steps, 1e-4 LR, 108 balanced samples).\n- **GPU:** Colab Tesla T4 (free tier). Local machine has GTX 1650 (4GB VRAM).\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n### A. Overfitting Diagnosis & Calibrated Retraining (COMPLETED)\n- Diagnosed original training: 60 steps, 5 epochs, loss collapsed to 0.0032 (severe overfitting with r=64, α=128, 0 benign samples).\n- Designed calibrated config: r=16, α=32, 25 steps, 2 epochs, LR=1e-4, 108 balanced samples (45 vuln + 35 benign + 28 identity).\n- Updated local files: `config/training_config.yaml`, `train.py`, `prepare_datasets.py`, `data/custom_cot/security_cot.jsonl`, `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb`.\n\n### B. NameError Resolution (COMPLETED)\n- Fixed `NameError: name 'FastLanguageModel' is not defined` in Colab S