urity** — models that can run locally, are small enough to fine-tune on consumer hardware, and are good at understanding code. Consider:\\n   - Microsoft Phi-3/Phi-4 mini\\n   - Google Gemma 2/3\\n   - Meta CodeLlama (smaller variants)\\n   - Mistral 7B / Codestral\\n   - Qwen 2.5 Coder\\n   - StarCoder2\\n   - DeepSeek Coder (small variants)\\n   - Any cybersecurity-specific fine-tuned models (SecBERT, CyberBERT, etc.)\\n   - Any other relevant SLMs\\n\\n2. For each model, provide:\\n   - Parameter count\\n   - Whether it's good at code understanding\\n   - Whether it can be fine-tuned for vulnerability detection\\n   - Hardware requirements\\n   - License (commercial use allowed?)\\n   - Any known cybersecurity fine-tunes or benchmarks\\n\\n3. **Cybersecurity datasets** for fine-tuning:\\n   - SARD (Software Assurance Reference Dataset)\\n   - CWE datasets\\n   - OWASP vulnerability samples\\n   - CVE databases\\n   - Any code vulnerability datasets on HuggingFace\\n   - Big-Vul, Devign, ReVeal, D2A datasets\\n\\n4. **Architecture recommendations** for building a vulnerability scanner:\\n   - Should it use RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) with a vulnerability knowledge base?\\n   - Should it use fine-tuning on vulnerability datasets?\\n   - Should it combine static analysis tools with LLM reasoning?\\n   - Best approach for different vulnerability types\\n\\nReturn a comprehensive summary with your top 3 SLM recommendations ranked.\",\n    \"inherit\":  true,\n    \"model\":  \"MODEL_PLACEHOLDER_M36\",\n    \"modelTier\":  \"MODEL_TIER_PRO\"\n  },\n  \"result\":  {\n    \"conversationId\":  \"8f1d6f42-1848-40b8-a147-8622731ef004\",\n    \"logAbsoluteUri\":  \"file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f1d6f42-1848-40b8-a147-8622731ef004/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\n    \"workspaceUris\":  [\n      \"file:///c%3A/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"spawnStepIndex\":  7\n}\n{\n  \"spec\":  {\n    \"typeName\":  \"bro