ON object specifying arguments like a file path.\n\nSince this is a major project, I want to sketch a directory structure first: an agent package with a core ReAct loop, an LLM interface wrapping Fluxnat Coder 3B, a memory module, a prompts module, and a tools subpackage with a base tool class.\n\nThe tools folder needs file operations, a code vulnerability scanner, a CVE/CWE lookup, sandboxed execution, git scanning, and report generation. Given I'm constrained to a 4GB GTX 1650, I need to figure out quantization strategy—4-bit via bitsandbytes/GPTQ, or llama-cpp-python with GGUF.\n\nThe full merged model on HF is 16-bit (~6GB), which won't fit, but quantizing to 4-bit brings it down to roughly 1.5-2GB, which should work fine. Since Ollama is off the table, I'll load the model with transformers and bitsandbytes 4-bit quantization instead. I'm leaning toward a ReAct-style agent loop over function calling, since that's simpler for a 3B model to handle reliably.","tool_calls":[{"name":"list_dir","args":{"DirectoryPath":"c:\\Users\\k4ran\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\smartAGENT","toolAction":"Exploring project structure","toolSummary":"SmartAGENT workspace"}}]}
